# Docker build context excludes. The build context is the repository root (see any Dockerfile).
#
# Keep this in sync with what the builds actually need: an over-broad pattern here surfaces as
# a missing-file error inside the container, not locally. In particular, do NOT add a blanket
# `**/*.md` — Xtzkt.Api/Swagger/description.md is an EmbeddedResource and the build fails
# without it.

# Build output and IDE state
**/bin
**/obj
**/publish
**/TestResults
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.*proj.user
**/*.dbmdl
**/*.jfm
**/.classpath
**/.project
**/.settings
**/.toolstarget

# Local secrets and environment
**/.env
/.env.example
**/*.pfx
**/secrets.dev.yaml
**/values.dev.yaml

# Docker and deployment descriptors — the image never needs its own build recipe
**/Dockerfile*
**/.dockerignore
**/docker-compose*
**/azds.yaml
**/charts

# Repo docs and agent/CI tooling
/README.md
/LICENSE
/CLAUDE.md
/CLAUDE.local.md
.claude
.github
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log

# Git metadata, except the few files the .NET SDK's built-in SourceLink reads to stamp the
# assembly with its repository URL and commit. These reach the SDK stages only — the final
# image copies just the publish output. .git/config holds the remote URL, so if a build ever
# runs in a clone whose remote embeds a token, drop the four exceptions below.
**/.git
!.git/HEAD
!.git/config
!.git/packed-refs
!.git/refs/heads/**
